wn":6.6,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":["paper"],"description_full":"Korn Ferry, together with its subsidiaries, engages in the provision of organizational consulting services worldwide. The company offers consulting services for talent strategies, organizational structures, and workforce capabilities; and develops, integrates, and commercializes with Korn Ferry Talent suite, as well as enabling technology across Korn Ferry's other solution areas. The company operates cloud human resources platforms comprising Korn Ferry Architect, for providing organization and talent planning architecture for an agile and future-focused workforce; Korn Ferry Assess, for empowering leaders to take actions that lead to business success; Korn Ferry Listen, for deploying engagement surveys and benchmark employee engagement; Korn Ferry Sell, for developing and replicating sales strategies; and Korn Ferry Pay, a self-service pay solution, that provides global data and insights needed in real-time to make decisions on employee compensation programs. It serves public and private companies, consumer markets, government and public services, financial services, healthcare, education, life sciences, industrial, technology, and specialties sectors. The company was formerly known as Korn/Ferry International and changed its name to Korn Ferry in January 2019. Korn Ferry was founded in 1969 and is based in Los Angeles, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Gary D. Burnison | President, CEO & Executive Director | Age 64 | Compensation: $4.1M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 8K people. Revenue per employee of $328K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 9%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $36K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 13\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Korn Ferry is a mid-cap industrials business with a $4.1B market cap on $2.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 22% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 13-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $324M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 11 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.49\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 15\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 5.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 10% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Trading at a 48% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 29% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 8/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","11 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Industrials peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Among the least levered in Industrials \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Financial quality scores above most Industrials peers"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"What Korn Ferry (KFY)'s Leadership Training Boom Means For Shareholders","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/commercial-services/nyse-kfy/korn-ferry/news/what-korn-ferry-kfys-leadership-training-boom-means-for-shar","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794557945.809,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.668,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Behavioral Patterns of KFY and Institutional Flows","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/16/Behavioral_Patterns_of_KFY_and_Institutional_Flows_110926062601_1794223561.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794223561.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.843,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Korn Ferry (KFY) Stock May Be Trading At A Discount To Earnings","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/commercial-services/nyse-kfy/korn-ferry/news/korn-ferry-kfy-stock-may-be-trading-at-a-discoun